{"name":"Red Baron","hex":"#bb0011","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Red Baron","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hotshot fighter pilot.","A red-coloured dragonfly, Urothemis aliena, family Libellulidae, of New Guinea and north and eastern Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Red_Baron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Baron (1990 video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Baron is a combat flight simulation video game for MS-DOS created by Damon Slye at Dynamix. It was published by Sierra On-Line in 1990. The game was ported for Amiga and Macintosh computers in 1992."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/Red_Baron_Coverart.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Baron_(1990_video_game)","wikidata":"Q476514"},{"title":"Red Baron (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Baron  is a Japanese animated television series directed by Akio Sakai and produced by Nippon TV along with Tokyo Movie Shinsha. The show is a remake of the 1973 live-action series Super Robot Red Baron."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Baron_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q3297634"},{"title":"Manfred von Richthofen","blocks":[{"text":"Rittmeister Manfred Albrecht Freiherr von Richthofen, known in English as Baron von Richthofen or the Red Baron, was a German fighter pilot with the German Air Force during World War I. He is considered the ace-of-aces of the war, being officially credited with 80 air combat victories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Manfred_von_Richthofen.jpg/330px-Manfred_von_Richthofen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manfred_von_Richthofen","wikidata":"Q4701"},{"title":"Baron","blocks":[{"text":"Baron is a rank of nobility or title of honour, often hereditary, in various European countries, either current or historical. The female equivalent is baroness. Typically, the title denotes an aristocrat who ranks higher than a lord or knight, but lower than a viscount or count. Often, barons hold their fief – their lands and income – directly from the monarch. Barons are less often the vassals of other nobles. In many kingdoms, they were entitled to wear a smaller form of a crown called a coronet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Heraldic_Crown_of_Spanish_Barons.svg/330px-Heraldic_Crown_of_Spanish_Barons.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron","wikidata":"Q165503"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/In_Red_Baron.JPG/330px-In_Red_Baron.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/In_Red_Baron.JPG/330px-In_Red_Baron.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gameplay screenshot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIn_Red_Baron.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Richthofen-Wappen.png/500px-Richthofen-Wappen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Richthofen-Wappen.png/500px-Richthofen-Wappen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Richthofen family coat of arms","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARichthofen-Wappen.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Lanoe_Hawker.jpg/250px-Lanoe_Hawker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/81/Lanoe_Hawker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/